From 9da06e6a3208d08d87236b8375566ac8e3b323e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:50:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/43] perf(sumcheck): fold subrelation separators into
 Poseidon2 quad relations on the prover

Poseidon2QuadInternal, Poseidon2QuadInternalTerminal and Poseidon2TransitionEntry
apply different constant linear maps to the same S-box outputs in each subrelation and
scale every subrelation by the same selector factor. SumcheckProverRound now hands
relations that opt in (SubrelationBatchingConstants) their subrelation separators
relative to the first one; such a relation accumulates the separator-weighted sum of its
subrelations into the first accumulator. Each S-box constant is folded into the degree-1
factor of x^5 = x^4 * x, so the per-row cost of the quad internal relation drops from
~320 to ~155 field multiplications. scale_univariates then multiplies by the first
separator, so the round univariate is unchanged. Verifier paths are untouched.
